## 2. What is an Operating System?

An Operating System (OS) is system software that manages computer hardware and provides services to applications.

### Main Responsibilities

1. Process Management.
2. Memory Management.
3. File Management.
4. Device Management.
5. Security Management.
6. Network Management.

### Examples

- Windows
- Linux
- macOS
- Android

### Linux vs Windows

| Linux | Windows |
|---|---|
| Open source | Proprietary |
| Commonly used in servers | Commonly used in desktops |
| Strong command-line tools | GUI-focused |
| Highly customizable | Comparatively less customizable |
| Many distributions | Different Windows editions |

