## 20. Cron Jobs and Task Scheduling

Cron is used to schedule commands or scripts to run automatically at specified times.

### Open Cron Configuration

```bash
crontab -e
```

### Cron Syntax

```text
* * * * * command
| | | | |
| | | | └── Day of week
| | | └──── Month
| | └────── Day of month
| └──────── Hour
└────────── Minute
```

### Examples

Run a script every day at 10 AM:

```bash
0 10 * * * /home/vboxuser/backup.sh
```

Run every 5 minutes:

```bash
*/5 * * * * /home/vboxuser/backup.sh
```

List scheduled jobs:

```bash
crontab -l
```

Remove scheduled jobs:

```bash
crontab -r
```

