## 23. Linux in Data Engineering

Linux is extremely important in Data Engineering because many Big Data tools run on Linux servers.

### Hadoop

Linux is commonly used to install and manage Hadoop clusters.

Commands:

```bash
start-dfs.sh
start-yarn.sh
```

### HDFS

Used to manage distributed data storage.

```bash
hdfs dfs -ls /
hdfs dfs -mkdir /data
hdfs dfs -put file.csv /data/
```

### YARN

Used to manage cluster resources and applications.

```bash
yarn application -list
```

### Hive

Hive provides SQL-based data querying.

Example:

```bash
beeline -u jdbc:hive2://localhost:10000
```

### Kafka

Kafka runs as a distributed event-streaming platform.

Linux is used to start, stop, and monitor Kafka services.

### Spark

Spark applications can be executed using Linux commands.

```bash
spark-submit application.py
```

